### CHAPTER IV

### COORDINATION AND COOPERATION

#### Article 16

1. The implementation of coordination and cooperation for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to: a. improve efforts to fulfill the rights of Women and Children;
b. improve synergistic and harmonious working relationships; and c. obtain data and information in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children.
2. In order to achieve the objectives as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with:
a. other Regional Governments;
b. related agencies;
c. non-governmental institutions;

d. universities; and
e. non-governmental organizations.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. socialization or legal counseling lectures;
c. rehabilitation of victims of violence; and d. repatriation and social reintegration.

##### CHAPTER V

##### RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

## Part One

General

#### Article 17

(1) The Regional Government is responsible for the protection of the rights of Women and Children.

III - 12 - (2) The responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) include: a. education;
b. health;
c. politics;
d. law;
e. economy;
f. culture; and g. social.
3. The responsibility of the Regional Government for the protection of the rights of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: a. formulation of gender-responsive Regional policies;
b. institutionalization of gender mainstreaming within the Regional Government;
c. empowerment of Women in the fields of politics, law, economy, culture and social affairs in city-level community organizations;
d. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Women's empowerment at the city level;
e. implementing efforts to prevent violence against Women.
4. The responsibility of the Regional Government for the protection of the rights of Children as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: a. formulation of policies, programs, and Regional development activities with a child rights perspective which are set forth in Regional development planning documents;
b. formulation of norms, standard procedures and evaluation criteria for the fulfillment and protection of Children's rights which refer to norms, standards, procedures and criteria established by the government;
c. implementation of child-friendly cities is carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
d. facilitation of the implementation of Regional Children's forums;
e. increasing community participation in the implementation and protection of Children's rights;
f. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of programs for the fulfillment and Protection of Children;

III - 13 -
g. guidance of Child Protection institutions;

h. providing special protection for Children; and i. implementing efforts to prevent violence against Children.

#### Article 18

(1) The Regional Government in carrying out the responsibility of institutionalizing Gender Mainstreaming as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (3) letter b regarding the Protection of Women and Children is obliged to organize an information system for Women and Children data.

2. The Women's data information system as referred to in paragraph (1) is an inseparable part of the Children's data information system.
3. The Women and Children information system as referred to in paragraph (2) is further regulated by Mayor Regulation.
4. Gender mainstreaming as referred to in paragraph (1) is organized in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

#### Article 19

1. In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of Protection of Women and Children, the Regional Government must carry out cross-sectoral coordination with related institutions.
2. In organizing the coordination of Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1), the Mayor establishes a coordination team for the Protection of Women and Children.

(3) In the coordination forum activities as referred to in paragraph (2), the coordination team for the Protection of Women and Children has the duties of: a. preparing materials needed related to the implementation of Protection of Women and Children; and
b. conveying results, obstacles, and solutions undertaken to overcome obstacles in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children.

III - 14 - (4) The coordination forum as referred to in paragraph (3) is conducted periodically, at least 2 (two) times in 1 (one) year.

## Part Two

Prevention of Violence Against Women and Children

#### Article 20

(1) The Regional Government is obliged and responsible to implement efforts to prevent violence against Women and Children as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (3) letter e and paragraph (4) letter i carried out in the form of:
a. collecting data and organizing an information system for the Protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
b. conducting education on anti-violence values against Women and Children; and c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the empowerment of Women and Protection of Children victims of violence.
